  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider a curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in the first quadrant as shown in the figure. Let the area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is twice the area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Then the normal to the curve perpendicular to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;does NOT pass through the point __</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0081_d6a7b1861028.png\" style=\"width: 373px; height: 250px;\" />​​​​​​​</p>"
  },
